        "text": "Re-Elect Dion Bailey Hercules City Council\nDonate\n# Steady leadership,\nstill working for Hercules.\nSince 2018, Dion Bailey has served Hercules on the City Council — strengthening public safety, investing in parks and recreation, and supporting local business. Now he's asking for a third term to keep that work going.\n26,000\nResidents of Hercules\n2\nTerms Served on Council\n3rd\nTerm Now Sought\n30\nYears a Hercules Resident\nAbout Dion\n## A familiar face, a proven record.\nSince 2018, Dion Bailey has served the residents of Hercules on the City Council, working to improve public safety, parks and recreation facilities, support local businesses, and protect the City's long-term financial stability. As former Hercules Planning Commissioner and civil servant, small business owner, and thirty-year Hercules resident, he brings years experience to the job.\nDion currently represents Hercules on the WestCAT Board of Directors, and serves on the City's Economic Development and Traffic & Public Safety subcommittees — advocating for reliable, accessible transit that meets the needs of commuters, seniors, families, and residents with disabilities.\nRunning for a third term isn't about starting over. It's about finishing what's already underway, with the institutional knowledge that comes from having done the job before.\n“I am committed to keeping Hercules a great place to live, work, and raise a family.”\nDion Bailey, Hercules City Council\nThe Platform\n## What Dion is focused on next.\nPriority\n### Public Safety\nContinuing to prioritize public safety investments so Hercules stays a place families are proud to call home.\nPriority\n### Parks & Recreation\nBuilding on recent upgrades to the gym and swim center, Refugio Valley Park's picnic areas, and Foxboro Park's courts and playground.\nPriority\n### Local Economy & Fiscal Responsibility\nSupporting small businesses through programs like the Shop Local Gift Card Program, while keeping Hercules on solid financial footing.\nPriority\n### Transit & Infrastructure\nAdvancing traffic calming on streets like Village Parkway and John Muir Parkway, pavement rehabilitation on Sycamore Avenue and Falcon Way, and reliable transit through the WestCAT Board.\nRecord of Service\n## Two terms of experience on the Hercules City Council.\n1\nFirst Term\n### 2018 – 2022\nElected after serving as a Hercules Planning Commissioner, bringing that experience to public safety and responsible growth from day one.\n2\nSecond Term\n### 2022 – 2026\nHelped launch the Shop Local Gift Card Program, advanced traffic calming on Village Parkway and John Muir Parkway, and voted to fund improvements at the gym and swim center, Refugio Valley Park, and Foxboro Park.\n3\nOn the Ballot\n### Third Term, 2026\nAsking Hercules voters for the opportunity to continue the work.\nEndorsed By\n## Local leaders who support Dion's re-election.\nShannell Scales-Preston\nContra Costa County Supervisor\nAlex Walker-Griffin\nHercules Vice Mayor\nTiffany Grimsley\nHercules Councilmember\nChris Kelley\nHercules Mayor\nDilli Bhattarai\nHercules Councilmember\nCameron Sasai\nPinole City Councilmember\nJamela Smith-Folds\nWCCUSD School Board Trustee\nLaura Nakamura\nConcord Mayor\nAmanda Szakats\nPleasant Hill City Councilmember\nBrianne Zorn\nMartinez Mayor\nRita Xavier\nSan Pablo Vice Mayor\nAnthony Tave\nPinole Mayor\nGabriel Quinto\nEl Cerrito Mayor\nShannon Sharp\nOakley Councilmember\nColin Coffee\nEast Bay Regional Park District Director\nSherry McCoy\nFormer Hercules Mayor\nMyrna de Vera\nFormer Hercules Mayor\nContra Costa Building & Construction Trades Council\nLabor Organization\nContra Costa Labor Council\nLabor Organization\nGet Involved\n## Hercules re-elects the people it trusts.\nWhether it's five dollars or five hours on a Saturday, every bit of support helps keep this campaign — and this city — moving forward.\nDonate Sign Up to Volunteer Get a Yard Sign\nSign Up for Updates\nFirst name Last name Email Zip/Postal Message\nThanks for signing up!\n- Privacy Policy\nDion Bailey for City Council 2026\nFPPC# 1494996\nPowered by CampaignPartner.com\n- Home\nClose Menu",
